      },
      "message": "fix(post): Explain G-code reads a lathe's own words - G98/G99 feed modes, T0101 tool 1 offset 1, G50 S speed limit\n\nThe PRELUDE's explain() had one word table, the mill reading, so a lathe\npost that opts in would say G98/G99 are cycle returns, T0101 is tool 101\nand G50 S3000 is a plain speed. A post now states its own meanings in\nits manifest: explainWords (a text, \"\" to stay silent, or { said, takes }\nfor a word explained only beside the value word it folds in) and\nexplainTool = \"station-offset\" (Txxyy: tool, then offset). fanuc-lathe\nstates G98/G99/G50 and the T reading, tormach-lathe the T reading. A\nmalformed table is refused by name when Explain is on; with Explain off\nnothing is read and the programs are byte-identical.\n\nPinned by explain_lathe.rs (fanuc-lathe posted with Explain on and off).\n\nFixes #1399\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
